# Eval run artifacts — commit the scorecards / stats / summary, never the
# verbose pipeline logs (tens of MB each) or raw stdout.
results/**/*.log
results/**/*.stdout
results/**/*.diag.json

# Ad-hoc / non-reference run labels. A results dir is committed only when it is
# a REFERENCE another run will be scored against; scratch verification runs and
# runs whose numbers are not gate-valid stay local. Listed explicitly rather
# than pattern-matched, because committed references live in this same
# directory and a broad rule would silently swallow the next one.
results/server-verify/
results/server-verify2/
# exp047's cache-pinned pre-check: every prompt was a replayed cache hit, so its
# src/ numbers are not gate-valid (measurement-pitfalls rule 10). Deliberately
# NOT a leaderboard peer — the cold legs exp047-cold-control / exp047-cold are.
# Its numbers are recorded in experiments/047-vendor-residual/RESULTS.md.
results/exp047-manifestorder/

# Single-pair probe legs. A label carrying a version (EVAL_PAIRS-scoped A/B runs
# such as exp054c-on-2.1.86) scores ONE hop, so it can never be a leaderboard
# reference — those are always four-pair and never carry a version in the label.
# Narrow enough not to swallow the next reference, which is what the explicit
# list above exists to protect. The numbers such runs produced belong in the
# experiment's RESULTS.md, not in a committed scorecard.
results/*-2.1.*/
